1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,538
We are Black Ant.

2
00:00:01,538 --> 00:00:10,000
We move Earth from 1 AU to 2.7 AU with a
gravity tractor that light holds in place.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:17,547
An asteroid of four times ten to the twenty
kilograms sits 637,100 km from Earth,

4
00:00:17,547 --> 00:00:19,811
and its gravity pulls Earth outward.

5
00:00:19,811 --> 00:00:25,849
Earth pulls back just as hard, and light
on the asteroid's mirror holds it in place.

6
00:00:25,849 --> 00:00:30,000
No beam comes within 420,000 km of Earth.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,226
Mars has to move first.

8
00:00:33,226 --> 00:00:47,419
Its own tow sprints across Jupiter's 2:1
resonance and parks it at 3.64 AU in year

9
00:00:47,419 --> 00:00:50,645
5,168.

10
00:00:50,645 --> 00:01:06,774
Then Earth crosses the asteroid belt, and
arrives at 2.7006 AU in year 8,758, inside

11
00:01:06,774 --> 00:01:10,000
the 10,000-year limit.

12
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:13,649
Mirrors in space keep Earth's
sunlight at today's level.

13
00:01:13,649 --> 00:01:20,946
All ten safety thresholds hold the whole
way: 288 K, liquid water on 82 percent of

14
00:01:20,946 --> 00:01:25,000
the surface, and the Moon well
inside Earth's Hill sphere.

15
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:29,875
Every force is booked with its reaction:
the stations' recoil, the bounced light,

16
00:01:29,875 --> 00:01:31,375
the asteroids sent away.

17
00:01:31,375 --> 00:01:38,500
The ledger closes to 5.6 times ten to the
minus 16, against the guide's limit of ten

18
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:40,000
to the minus 9.

19
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:46,000
With the tows gone, we ran the new
solar system for a million years.

20
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Earth stays between 2.698 and 2.702
AU, and nothing is thrown out.

21
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:04,600
We audited the reference concept too: its
arms push only on Earth's own core, and a

22
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:10,000
12,000 km arm buckles
under its own weight.

23
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:13,125
All ten official benchmarks pass.

24
00:02:13,125 --> 00:02:20,000
The code, the report and this
test bench are on GitHub.
